     "text": [
      "Cayley–Menger area² for sides a, b, c:\n    -(((c-b-a)*(c-b+a)*(c+b-a)*(c+b+a))/16)\nHeron's formula   :  -(((c-b-a)*(c-b+a)*(c+b-a)*(c+b+a))/16)\ndifference        :  0   — identical\nregular-ish tetrahedron with vertices at the origin and the three unit points\nedge lengths     :  [1,1,1,sqrt(2),sqrt(2),sqrt(2)]\nCayley–Menger V² :  1/36   → V =  1/6\ndirect  |det|/6  :  1/6\nfour mutually-unit-distant points: V² =\n  1/72   (positive — a regular tetrahedron of edge 1, so realisable in R³)\ntriangle with sides 1, 1, 3: area² =  -(45/16)\n                                       (negative — violates the triangle inequality, no such triangle)"
     ]
    }
