     "text": [
      "distance matrix, original:\nmatrix([0,2,sqrt(37)/2,3*sqrt(2)],[2,0,(3*sqrt(5))/2,3*sqrt(2)],\n       [sqrt(37)/2,(3*sqrt(5))/2,0,9/2],[3*sqrt(2),3*sqrt(2),9/2,0])\ndistance matrix, mirrored:\nmatrix([0,2,sqrt(37)/2,3*sqrt(2)],[2,0,(3*sqrt(5))/2,3*sqrt(2)],\n       [sqrt(37)/2,(3*sqrt(5))/2,0,9/2],[3*sqrt(2),3*sqrt(2),9/2,0])\nidentical?  true\nsigned volume, original:  4\nsigned volume, mirrored:  -4\n→ same |V|, opposite sign: congruent in E(3), NOT in SE(3)\nCayley–Menger V² of each:  16   and   16\nas it must be — it is a function of distances, so it is blind to chirality"
